   "unmapped": [
    "Queueing system: N queues (agents) with Bernoulli job arrivals at unknown rates lambda_n; K servers (arms); queue lengths evolve with the learner's assignments (state-dependent system).",
    "Each round the scheduler partitions non-empty queues into disjoint assortments of size at most L per server; only non-empty queues can be assigned.",
    "Service probability given by a feature-based multinomial logit (MNL) model with known agent features x_n and unknown server parameters theta_k; each server serves at most one assigned job (MNL choice / preference feedback).",
    "Objectives: average queue length (stability) and queue-weighted regret against the MaxWeight oracle.",
    "Traffic slackness assumption with parameter epsilon (Assumption 3).",
    "Regularity constant kappa (Assumption 2) known to the learner; L known to the learner."
   ],
   "definition_quote": "There are $N$ agents (queues) and $K$ arms (servers). At each time, a job for each agent $n\\in [N]$ arrives randomly following a Bernoulli distribution with an unknown arrival rate $\\lambda_n\\in[0,1]$ ... arm $k$ serves a job of agent $n\\in S_{k,t}$ with a service probability (service rate) determined by the MNL model as \\[\\mu(n|S_{k,t},\\theta_k)=\\frac{\\exp(x_n^\\top \\theta_k)}{1+\\sum_{m\\in S_{k,t}}\\exp(x_m^\\top \\theta_k)}.\\]"
  },
